                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">9. VOLUME

The VOLUME instruction creates a mount point inside the container and is used for persistent or
shared data storage.

Example:

1. If you define a single argument, it creates a volume inside a container.

  VOLUME [&quot;/shared-data&quot;]



2. If you define multiple arguments, it creates multiple volumes inside the container.

  VOLUME [&quot;/volume1&quot;, &quot;/volume2&quot;]</pre>
